Z||000000||Turkey on Rye||10-17-2001||04:16 PM||||I am in the market for some new wheels for my car. I found some cool 5-star wheels but they are a 15 x 6" wheel.  Now i know that my stock wheel i have now is a 15 x 7" wheel.  Is there anyway around this or will i just have to find a 15 x 7" wheel?  Thanks for any help!<BR>             -Chris<BR>P.S. I'm keepin my original tires.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-17-2001||10:30 PM||||As long as the offset and bolt pattern are the same, I think you can put any rim on a Fiero, diameter limited.  Don't know if you will still want to use your stock tires though if your rim is going to be that much smaller, might look weird.<P>Anyways, look for some more info by doing a search in both the technical discussion and the general Fiero chat sections.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jefrysuko||10-18-2001||12:17 AM||||I like your name.  Is that what you eat for lunch every day or is there something else behind that?  Just curious.<P>Just for your info.  The 14" rims that come stock on SE's etc are only 6" wide.  So if you are worrried about the way they will look don't they are plenty wide but will just be slightly inside the fenders where as that stock ones are slightly outside.  This is assuming they are the correct offset.||||reg||1
